{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgArKtm4u61sXjQQe9Qen","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The deploy script now sets `Cache-Control` on every upload, and I wrote up the change in `ANSWER.md`. I haven't deployed, so the live site still serves the old headers until the first real run.\n\n- **Short cache (`max-age=300`)** for `*.html`, `*.js` and `*.css`. I included CSS because `styles.css` is at the root, not in `assets/`.\n- **Long cache (`max-age=86400`)** for `assets/*.png` and `assets/*.svg`. I used one day rather than a year because the asset filenames aren't fingerprinted, so a changed logo would otherwise stay stale for a year.\n- **Content types** are set alongside the cache policy, so an upload can't go out with only one of them.\n\nI didn't follow the guide's copy-onto-self loop. The script now re-uploads each file type from the local `src/` with the content type and cache policy stated explicitly. That avoids `--metadata-directive REPLACE` entirely. The reason for not using plain `sync` is that it skips unchanged files, so it would never add headers to objects already in the bucket. The deploy also stops before uploading anything if `src/` contains a file type the script has no content type for.\n\n**Verification:** I ran the script with a stub `aws` that only prints its arguments, and the sequence was correct. I also dry-ran the include filters against the real `src/`, and all six files matched. I did not run the live `curl -sI` checks because they need a real deploy.\n\nChanges are uncommitted in `scripts/deploy.sh` and `ANSWER.md`. The README's \"Known problem\" note is still accurate until the first deploy with this script, so I left it alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1554,"cache_read_input_tokens":31266,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_